{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqs2cryemhg","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Fresh memory-bench run: LoCoMo + LongMemEval-Oracle on enrich+grader defaults (sample-first)","summary":"Re-measuring the agent-memory bench (arms: our-way / search / cold) on real LoCoMo (10 convs, 1986 probes) + LongMemEval-Oracle (500 convs/probes) now that (1) the P4 SDK migration is MERGED — probe_runner routes our-way→arms.run_retrieve_and_answer and dag-combined→arms.run_canonical_wiring, driving the production judge via POST /judge/drain — and (2) enrich + LLM grader are the production default (commit e059d3a6). SDK smoke PASS 3/3 on current main. KEY CONSTRAINT (extends note-mqq2d9u1f7x): the bench ANSWERER (bench/zonoid_bench/judge.py claude_p) is CLI-only — spawns claude -p per probe at ~1-1.5 min/call, no API completion path in the SDK — so a full 2486-probe x 3-arm run is ~20+ hours. Therefore running a SAMPLE first (Oracle --limit 10; LoCoMo 1 conv x 10 probes) to get a first number + measure true per-probe cost before committing to the full sweep. Competitor comparison is PUBLISHED bars (mem0/Zep/H-MEM LoCoMo+LongMemEval), NOT live arms. Datasets downloaded to C:/Users/Imyu/.cache/zmbench/data (NOT committed; LoCoMo CC BY-NC, LongMemEval MIT). Worktree-based orch attempt flow is currently broken on this Windows box (core.longpaths unset -> MAX_PATH on long .graph/nodes/knowledge%3A... filenames); sample run needs no claim since curl/python writes are ungated.","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-24T12:42:39.110Z","vec":[-0.08298567682504654,0.04170907288789749,-0.05779748037457466,-0.009978285990655422,0.01977614127099514,-0.10712896287441254,-0.06592243164777756,0.08797761797904968,-0.031000513583421707,0.032220516353845596,-0.0023770418483763933,-0.07300989329814911,0.037452854216098785,-0.0528579019010067,0.016626277938485146,0.03761202096939087,0.04202203452587128,0.032315444201231,-0.07167176157236099,0.002679952885955572,0.049755316227